[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3785185470","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115220#issuecomment-3785185470","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115220","id":3785185470,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hnVi-","user":{"login":"JerryLin1","id":21973246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTczMjQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21973246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1","html_url":"https://github.com/JerryLin1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T15:56:30Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T16:22:09Z","body":"Sorry, first time contributing and didn't know about these unit tests. It's failing on some drag and drop tests and \"Mouse Enter/Exit notification when hiding the hovered Control\", which is definitely very related to the bug I'm trying to fix. Regarding the latter test, it appears that the unit test is expecting the old behaviour and should be updated? \r\n\r\n<img width=\"912\" height=\"189\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8379cfa0-ff95-42aa-b1d7-e6cb677f79ae\" />\r\n\r\nThe test is expecting that if a node is underneath a hovered node that becomes hidden, the node underneath should not fire mouse_entered (e.g. When red panel disappears, blue panel is entered). This is technically a bit different from what the original issue discussed but it's in the same vein, and I think it would be much more intuitive if this unit test was updated to expect mouse_entered. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3785185470/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3785419356","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115220#issuecomment-3785419356","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115220","id":3785419356,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hoOpc","user":{"login":"kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev","html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T16:41:46Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T16:41:46Z","body":"The test is there to make sure the behavior is consistent between showing and hiding, and to make sure that behavior changes are intentional. So the test can be updated here.\r\nI am not sure why the tab tests would be failing here though.\r\n\r\nDoes this also work when adding and removing the Control instead of just changing visibility?\r\nIf so, we may also want to update it when its child order changes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/40012 (mentioned in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/84547#issuecomment-1802569332) but that may be more complex.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3785419356/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3785549986","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115220#issuecomment-3785549986","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115220","id":3785549986,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7houii","user":{"login":"JerryLin1","id":21973246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTczMjQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21973246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1","html_url":"https://github.com/JerryLin1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T17:05:33Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T17:08:35Z","body":"Yea I'm still looking into the tab tests, but I wonder if it's because of some quirk with the way that unit tests simulate mouse inputs that differs from how they behave normally, that causes a discrepancy in `get_mouse_position`. I'm still trying to familiarize myself with the code though.\n\nBut thank you for bringing up these other issues, ideally a fix should cover them as well I think.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3785549986/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3814905808","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115220#issuecomment-3814905808","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115220","id":3814905808,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jYtfQ","user":{"login":"JerryLin1","id":21973246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTczMjQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21973246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1","html_url":"https://github.com/JerryLin1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-29T01:53:23Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T01:53:23Z","body":"I've fixed the issues, and updated the viewport unit test to reflect the new behaviour. Sorry for the mess of commits, still getting used to the workflow.\r\nThe mouse_entered/mouse_exited signals get emitted when visibility changes, when control nodes are added/removed from the tree, and now when child order is changed (closing #40012).\r\n\r\nHowever, at the moment it still does not work as expected when changing z_index order, but I'm not sure if this would be a separate issue so I'm opting to leave it alone for now. The existing behaviour seems to be that z_index does not affect which control node gets mouse_entered/mouse_exited at all, instead it depends on node order in the tree only. So a control node that is on top of another due to having a higher z_index does not get mouse_entered if the control node below it is lower in the scene tree. This looks very weird to me, but maybe I'm mistaken?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3814905808/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3816352481","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115220#issuecomment-3816352481","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115220","id":3816352481,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jeOrh","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-29T08:56:40Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T08:56:40Z","body":"Please avoid pushing so many times to your branch, as a first time contributor you need permission to run the CI but if you weren't this would have taken up a lot of processing unnecessarily ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3816352481/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3828834734","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115220#issuecomment-3828834734","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115220","id":3828834734,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kN2Gu","user":{"login":"JerryLin1","id":21973246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTczMjQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21973246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1","html_url":"https://github.com/JerryLin1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JerryLin1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/